    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0435" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1142: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-04T17:00:00+01:00">November 4, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 4—1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7652. Reference Embassy’s 7239, October 21, 1 p.m. This morning’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Daily Sketch</hi> carried a brief item to the effect
                    that the Soviet Government had appointed a representative to the United Nations
                    Commission for the Investigation of War Crimes and that this altered its
                    previous decision not to be represented.</p>
                <p>A high official of the Foreign Office has informed the Embassy that as far as he
                    is aware the situation has not changed from that previously reported and that
                    negotiations are still in progress with the Soviet Government on this question.
                    He expressed the opinion that the author of the item in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Daily Sketch</hi> had misinterpreted the meaning of the
                    Moscow declaration on punishment of German war criminals.<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d437-f1"/> The Foreign Office will keep the Embassy informed of
                    developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
